-- A phase-changing single-cell depletion, which the compositional execution plan's C12 asks for
-- as a separate fixture from the 1D displacement. The PROPS section is 1D_COMP.DATA's verbatim:
-- same three components, same Peng-Robinson data, same SGOF, same surface conditions.
--
-- One cell, initially single-phase liquid at 150 bar (the mixture saturates between 100 and 125
-- bar at this temperature), produced at a FIXED SURFACE OIL RATE until
-- it falls through its saturation pressure and gas appears. Rate control rather than BHP control
-- is the point of the case: with the withdrawal imposed identically on both simulators, the
-- comparison is of the pressure path and the phase-appearance time, and it does not inherit the
-- conditioning that makes a near-shut-in well's cumulative a small difference of large numbers.
--
-- THE REFERENCE RUN ABORTS, DELIBERATELY KEPT. flowexp_comp depletes this cell cleanly to 111.55
-- bar single phase, produces one report step at 109.10 bar with gas just appeared (Sg = 0.0036),
-- and then its own Rachford-Rice fails to converge and the run is abandoned. Every two-phase
-- flash method it offers (ssi, newton, ssi-newton) fails the same way, and halving the production
-- rate only moves where. So the oracle cannot follow this case past its own saturation pressure,
-- and the fixture is seven report steps rather than twenty. Those seven are what matters: they
-- cover the single-phase depletion path AND the phase appearance itself, which is what C12 asks
-- this fixture to compare.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   SINGLE CELL DEPLETION

METRIC

TABDIMS
/
OIL
GAS
DIMENS
1 1 1
/

COMPS
3 /

WELLDIMS
1 1 1* 1/

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT
------------------------------------------------------------------------
